<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">United Provinces of the Río de la Plata</h1><p class="st-meta">1810 CE – 1831 CE · capital Buenos Aires</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The revolutionary state formed in Buenos Aires in 1810 that declared independence from Spain in 1816 and became the core of Argentina.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The May Revolution of 25 May 1810 replaced the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/viceroyalty-of-the-rio-de-la-plata">Viceroyalty of the Río de la Plata</a> with a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primera-junta">Primera Junta</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a>. Armies were sent to spread the revolution, but <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-paraguay">Paraguay</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/royal-audiencia-of-charcas">Upper Peru</a> resisted, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montevideo">Montevideo</a> held out for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> until 1814.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Government passed from juntas to triumvirates and, from 1814, Supreme Directors. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-belgrano">Manuel Belgrano</a> created the blue and white flag in 1812, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assembly-of-the-year-xiii">Assembly of the Year XIII</a> abolished titles and freed children born to enslaved mothers. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-tucuman">Congress of Tucumán</a> declared independence on 9 July 1816. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-de-san-martin">José de San Martín's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/army-of-the-andes">Army of the Andes</a> liberated <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-chile">Chile</a> in 1817 and 1818. Conflict between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buenos-aires">Buenos Aires</a> and federalist provinces, such as those of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/federal-league">Federal League</a>, was constant.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-cepeda-1820">Battle of Cepeda</a> in 1820 central government collapsed. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernardino-rivadavia">Bernardino Rivadavia's</a> presidency and a war with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/new-republic-brazil">Brazil</a> over <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cisplatina">Cisplatina</a> followed. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-pact">Federal Pact</a> of 1831 created the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/argentine-confederation">Argentine Confederation</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/united-provinces-of-the-rio-de-la-plata.jpg" alt="United Provinces of the Río de la Plata" width="320" height="201"><figcaption>Image: Juan Martín de Pueyrredón (1777-1850), according to Ministerio del Interior website (vector graphics by Guilherme Paula) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Argentina_(1818).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1810 CE – 1831 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Buenos Aires</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Cornelio Saavedra, Juan Martín de Pueyrredón, Bernardino Rivadavia</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Spanish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/argentina">Argentina</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>United Provinces of South America, United Provinces of the River Plate</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1820&amp;focus=united-provinces-of-the-rio-de-la-plata" aria-label="United Provinces of the Río de la Plata on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="3197 3430 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where United Provinces of the Río de la Plata lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3517 3686L3517 3686M3517 3686L3440 3589M3517 3686L3505 3614M3